# Terrain and placement share one grid, so the board is what it looks like.
#   .  open        #  wall        O  pit        ^  spikes      H  high ground
#   A  Player A deploy slot       B  Player B deploy slot
#   any other letter = an enemy declared by a 'spawn' line below

id: ec-04-bodies-and-rain
number: 304
name: Bodies and Rain
description: A trench with two one-tile bridges, a Husk standing on each, and Lobbers behind who shoot straight over them. The bodies stop your feet; they do not stop the rocks.
design: Enemy composition 4 — Husks own the bridges, Lobbers ignore the bridges entirely.
retired: Same trench-and-two-bridges board as `ec-08`, which asks the better question on it.

spawn h = Husk
spawn l = Lobber

roster a: Vanguard, Archer
roster b: Threadcaster, Wardbearer

board:
  .l.h.l.
  OOhOhOO
  .......
  .H...H.
  .......
  A.^.^.B
  AA...BB
